.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-submit - Verify, sign and submit a prepared payout


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts submit  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign a pending payout prepared earlier ('payouts prepare') and hand it to the
gateway, which broadcasts it.

.PP
The transaction is checked against the destination, read again from the gateway —
exactly transfer(destination address, payout amount) on the destination's token
and chain, value 0, from your key's wallet — and refused otherwise before the key
touches it. The command shows the amount, token, deposit address and network and
asks to confirm (y/N); --yes skips it and is required without a terminal.

.PP
Only a pending, unsigned payout can be signed. One already signed is 'resend's:
its transaction may already be in a mempool, and signing again would risk a second
transfer.

.PP
-w/--wait follows the payout until confirmed or failed, as in 'payouts send'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for submit

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	The destination wallet's key: 0x hex, @name for an OS-keychain key ('rail0 keys add'), or RAIL0_PRIVATE_KEY

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set; unset, 10× the chain's measured p90 settlement, kept within 5m–15m

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts submit <payout_id> -p @merchant-key
  rail0 payouts submit <payout_id> -p @merchant-key --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts(1)\fP
